\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\tab We have not known Thee as we ought,
\par \pard\li720 Nor learned Thy wisdom, grace, and power ;
\par The things of earth have filled our thought,
\par And trifles of the passing hour:
\par Lord, give us light Thy truth to see,
\par And make us wise in knowing Thee.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.\tab We have not feared Thee as we ought,
\par \pard\li720 Nor bowed beneath Thine awful eye,
\par Nor guarded deed, and word, and though,
\par Remembering that God was nigh ;
\par Lord, give us faith to know Thee near,
\par And grant the grace of holy fear.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.\tab We have not loved Thee as we ought,
\par \pard\li720 Nor cared that we are loved by Thee ;
\par Thy presence we have coldly sought,
\par And feebly longed Thy face to see ;
\par Lord, give a pure loving heart
\par To feel and know the love Thou art.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.\tab We have not served Thee as we ought ;
\par \pard\li720 Alas the duties left undone,
\par The work with little fervour wrought,
\par The battles lost or scarcely won !
\par Lord, give the zeal, and give the might,
\par For Thee to toil, for Thee to fight.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.\tab When shall we know Thee as we ought,
\par \pard\li720 And fear, and love, and serve aright ?
\par When shall we, out of trial brought,
\par Be perfect in the land of light ?
\par Lord, may we day by day prepare
\par To see Thy face and serve Thee there.
\par Amen.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

